PPROC(1)                       ZOAU Command Syntax                      PPROC(1)

NAME
	pproc - Display a PROCLIB concatenation.

SYNOPSIS

	pproc [-adh] [<proclib>]

	-a
		Display all proclibs.

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

DESCRIPTION

	Displays the various datasets within a proclib concatenation, or all of
	them if -a is specified.
	Without the <proclib> argument, it defaults to displaying PROC00 on JES2 
	and IATPLBST on JES3 systems. A different default name can be defined with
	the DEFAULT_PROC environment variable.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

	DEFAULT_PROC
		Overrides the default library name to be used when pproc is called
		without arguments.

EXAMPLES

	Displays PROC00.

		pproc

	Displays a user-defined default PROC10.

		export DEFAULT_PROC=PROC10
		pproc

	Displays PROC99.

		pproc PROC99

	Displays PROC00, PROC99, etc.

		pproc -a

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Success

	Other
		Error, see message for details

SEE ALSO

	pll(1), pparm(1)
	